#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:1
msgid "ADR-0013: Script blocks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-17"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P11.5 (REQ-PIPE-6, NF-7)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:9
msgid ""
"Processing pipelines need steps that LUMOS does not provide: a user "
"function placed in the graph with declared ports (REQ-PIPE-6). The same "
"contexts are saved in `.lumos` files, shared, loaded by the web instance "
"and by the MCP server; loading a file must never run code from it (NF-7, "
"no arbitrary imports)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:13
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:15
msgid ""
"`lumos.processing.script.script(name=..., inputs=..., outputs=...)` turns"
" a function into an `Element` subclass registered under `name`, like any "
"element type. Inputs are passed positionally in the declared order; the "
"function returns a mapping of outputs (or the signal of a single output)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:18
msgid ""
"Keyword-only arguments with defaults become the parameters: quantities "
"make `Param`s with units, `bool`, `int`, `float` and `str` make "
"`Setting`s. They are saved, edited and swept like other parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:20
msgid ""
"A `.lumos` file stores the type identifier and the parameter values only."
" Loading needs the script to be defined beforehand, by importing the "
"module that defines it or through the `lumos.elements` entry points of a "
"plugin package; otherwise loading fails with `UnknownTypeError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:23
msgid ""
"Defining again a script with the same name and the same function (module "
"and qualified name), as when a notebook cell runs twice, replaces the "
"registration; another function under the same name is refused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:26
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:28
msgid ""
"Storing the source code in the `.lumos` file and executing it on load: "
"arbitrary code execution from shared files, forbidden by NF-7."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:30
msgid ""
"Storing an import path (`module:function`) and importing it on load: an "
"arbitrary import chosen by the file, also forbidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:32
msgid ""
"Per-instance ports on a single generic `ScriptBlock` class: every element"
" type would no longer have fixed ports, which the JSON Schema, the web "
"palette and the codegen rely on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:35
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:37
msgid ""
"Scripts are visible in the registry, the web palette and the JSON Schema "
"once defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:38
msgid ""
"Sharing a context that uses scripts requires sharing the code that "
"defines them (a module or a plugin)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0013-script-blocks.md:39
msgid ""
"The web interface does not offer to type code in the browser; scripts "
"come from Python."
msgstr ""

